From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:38:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a Claude conversation's session waits out a restart
 on the shelf (#5971)

Every conversation that had a run waits for its next turn in a run of
its own, and the runs let go past idleMost leave their sessions on the
shelf - both only in the gateway's memory. After a restart, its own
update's handover included, nothing mapped a conversation to a session:
its next turn went to a new Claude Code from a transcript of the whole
conversation (replaySession), a prefix Anthropic's cache has never
seen, so every open conversation wrote itself to the prompt cache
again, only Claude Code's own system prompt and tools read back.

The shelf is now a file beside the providers' list (claude-shelf.json),
written at each change of the shelf: a run let go onto it, one taken
off (unshelve), one retired (retire), one waited out. The gateway
shelves every waiting run as it ends, before its runs are aborted, and
magpie ending on a signal shelves them too (ShelveIdle) - a quit and a
handover both reach one of the two. A turn that finds no run reads the
file (loadShelf) and goes on from the session its run cached, told the
turn alone, dropping entries past what their run would have waited
(idleLongest: the cache is gone either way) and ones this magpie took
(another magpie's final write may still have them). A session whose
file is gone resumes as nothing, a transcript as before.

The sweep at the next start spares them: an entry is only kept while
its run would have waited, and a session file newer than that is never
swept.

Ablations: without loadShelf the restart tests fail at "did not resume
its session after the restart"; without shelveIdle,
TestClaudeWaitingRunsShelveForTheRestart fails the same way while
TestClaudeShelfWaitsOutTheRestart passes (its session was shelved by
the idleMost overflow, not by the quit); without the stale-entry drop
(its expiry timer neutralized with it, else the timer's immediate fire
races the lookup), the stale entry is resumed past what its run would
have waited. Whole, all pass.

Run at upstream/main db0f2f20d + this commit, macOS 15 (darwin/arm64):
TestClaudeShelfWaitsOutTheRestart, TestClaudeWaitingRunsShelveForTheRestart,
TestClaudeRestartDropsStaleShelfEntries, TestClaudeSweepSparesShelvedSessions,
TestClaudeLetGoConversationResumesItsSession, TestClaudeSessionFilesAreRemoved,
TestClaudeOldSessionsAreSwept, TestClaudeAsideLeavesTheConversationsRun
(-tags nogui, -race too) ok.

Reported-by: Suge8
